 request(updates,'UPDATE-02','Confirmed','Always display the currently installed application version in the lower-left sidebar. When a newer release is available to download, indicate its availability in that same lower-left area and provide access to the download/update action. Continue showing the installed version while an update is available or downloaded; only an applied update changes that displayed current version.')
 request(updates,'UPDATE-03','Proposed','Distinguish update checking, available, downloading, staged, applying and failed states. Resolve the correct OS/CPU release asset, validate version and artifact integrity, show progress and retry/cancel where applicable, and preserve the working installed version on failed download or preparation. Update the bundled local Help with the corresponding app version. Preserve work/state and existing shutdown/manual-resume rules during installation/restart; self-improvement activation still requires explicit approval under SELF-03. Automatic background download and approval before installation/restart are confirmed under UPDATE-04. The architecture adopts stable releases by default with explicit prerelease opt-in, due launch/hourly checks, signed staging and approved installation/restart. Native offline/rate-limit, signature and platform installation/rollback qualification remains required.')
 request(updates,'UPDATE-04','Confirmed','Automatically download newly available application updates in the background. Require explicit user approval before installing the update and restarting the app. Release discovery or a completed download must not count as that approval. While approval is pending or declined, retain the running installed version and allow existing authorized work to continue. Apply approved updates with the existing work-preservation, shutdown and selective-resume rules; include the matching local Help version.')
 for b in find('23 ')['blocks']:
  if b[0]=='table':b[2].append(['GitHub release updates','With SceneWorks/DevWorks configured as the product release repository, verify hourly checks while the app is open and a persistent installed-version label in the lower-left sidebar across normal screens. Publish a newer compatible test release and verify the availability/download indicator appears there while the current-version label remains unchanged. Exercise download/preparation failures without replacing the working installation. Verify the compatible update downloads automatically in the background. Withhold or decline approval: installation/restart must not occur and existing authorized work may continue. Approve installation/restart, then apply the release and verify the installed version and local Help match afterward, with work retained and existing approval/resume rules honored. UPDATE 01–04; HELP 05; SELF 03; CONTROL 08–10.'])
 # User supplied document knowledge and retrieval augment the unified Knowledge system.
 rag=sec('24 Document knowledge and retrieval','Built-in document retrieval augmented generation is required. Users can add their own knowledge documents, index their content into searchable vectors and retrieve relevant passages through the app and agent tools. This extends the unified Knowledge system; a document corpus is source evidence rather than a separate memory, lesson or claim catalog. Plain SQLite and sqlite-vec are the selected app storage. The details marked Proposed below require review.')
 request(rag,'RAG-01','Confirmed','Provide a built-in RAG system for knowledge from documents: ingest document content, generate and store searchable vector representations, and retrieve relevant document passages for agents and human search. Users must be able to add knowledge documents of their own and have those documents indexed. This must not be limited to developer-shipped Help, convention pages, existing code indexes or externally hosted corpora.')
 request(rag,'RAG-02','Proposed','Expose a Documents area within the Knowledge workspace, backed by the same document ingestion and retrieval operations available through configured agent tools. Support adding local files using a selection dialog or drag and drop, inspecting source text and indexing status, searching the corpus, opening a result at its source passage, reindexing, disabling and removing a document from active retrieval. Include explicit sharing and Move to project controls under RAG-11. Show title, source, tags, project/shared scope, version, indexed time, chunk counts and errors. Imported documents are managed project artifacts under RAG-12. Removing an index must not silently delete an external original or the retained managed artifact; artifact deletion follows the existing explicit deletion and shared-reference rules. A chat attachment is not automatically a durable corpus document unless explicitly added or covered by a configured ingestion rule.')
 request(rag,'RAG-03','Proposed','Use a staged pipeline for supported document formats: extract text and structural locators, normalize it, split it into meaningful bounded chunks, generate embeddings through the internal router, and publish searchable chunks with source provenance. Markdown, plain text, PDF and Word documents are required under RAG-09. Initial Word ingestion supports modern .docx only under RAG-09; native extraction adapters remain to qualify. Routed vision fallback for scanned pages is confirmed under RAG-10. Report unsupported or encrypted sources and failed extraction honestly rather than marking empty content successfully indexed. Folder watching, remote URL ingestion and additional formats remain open choices; no mandatory preinstalled Node, Python or office runtime may be introduced into core use.')
 request(rag,'RAG-09','Confirmed','Support user-added Markdown, plain text, PDF and Word documents for knowledge ingestion, indexing and retrieval. These four document formats are required initial capabilities, not optional future formats. Apply the same indexing visibility, source provenance, project scope and agent retrieval requirements to each. Initial Word support is modern .docx only; legacy binary .doc is excluded from initial support. Scanned or image-only pages use the configurable routed vision fallback under RAG-10. Do not silently report failed or empty extraction as successful indexing.')
 request(rag,'RAG-10','Confirmed','Extract existing document text directly where available, and use a configured vision-capable model through the internal router as the fallback for scanned or image-only pages. Enable this vision extraction fallback by default. Expose the fallback and its model/route configuration in Settings, with enable/disable control. This pathway must not require a separate bundled OCR model or local inference runtime; a user-selected local vision endpoint may have its own optional runtime. Save the extracted text with the source document revision/content hash, page identity and extraction model provenance, preserving access to the original page. Reuse that extraction for indexing and retrieval until the source changes or re-extraction is explicitly requested, rather than repeating vision inference on each search. Chunking and embedding remain separate subsequent steps, and their inference also goes through the router. Show extraction progress, usage/costs and failures; if fallback is disabled or no capable route is available, mark affected pages as requiring extraction or partially indexed rather than silently claiming completion. Page rendering/batching, language coverage and quality acceptance remain to confirm.')
 request(rag,'RAG-04','Proposed','Offer hybrid lexical and vector retrieval so exact names, identifiers and terms remain searchable alongside semantic matches. Return bounded passages with source identity, revision/content hash, chunk identity and heading, page or other supported locator. Rank and deduplicate results, expose the retrieval mode and useful score information without presenting a similarity score as factual confidence. Where evidence supports a generated answer, provide navigable source citations; preserve retrieved source revisions and citations in the session/work history. Do not invent evidence when the corpus has no suitable result. Graph expansion linking documents to code, entities, features or tasks is a candidate enhancement; the precise ranking, fusion, reranking and graph traversal policy remains open.')
 request(rag,'RAG-05','Proposed','Enforce existing project/shared Knowledge scope and tool permissions before materializing retrieved content, including vector candidates, snippets, graph expansion and caches. Adding a document must not make it available across every project merely because it is indexed or tagged as a lesson. Show its effective scope; default project association, explicit sharing and moving are confirmed under RAG-11. Scope changes must reconcile retrieval filters and caches so former project associations do not continue granting future access. Exact sharing representation and update consistency mechanics remain to specify. Preserve the distinction between source text, derived claims and verified knowledge. Retrieved text is evidence and cannot override user directions, role authority or configured tool permissions. Database schema indexing remains metadata-only; this document requirement does not authorize importing database row values.')
 request(rag,'RAG-06','Proposed','Track source identity/content hash, extraction/chunking version, embedding model identity/revision and vector dimensions. Reuse unchanged valid chunks, reconcile edited and removed sources, and avoid mixing incompatible embedding spaces after a model change. Keep failed, partial, stale and completed indexing distinguishable with per-document and per-run logs, progress, cancellation and retry. Publish complete replacements without silently serving mixed source revisions; define retention of prior versions under existing artifact/history rules. Reopening the app must preserve the corpus, completed indexes and attributable interrupted operations; exact checkpoint and rebuild mechanics remain to specify.')
 request(rag,'RAG-07','Proposed','All embedding, query embedding, model-based extraction, reranking, summarization and answer generation must follow the internal router whenever they perform inference, including any reused library or package. Show effective models, provider availability, attributable usage/costs and failures. Precomputed local vector and lexical search must not require a separate database server. If an embedding provider is unavailable, expose reduced lexical-only retrieval where supported rather than claiming vector search succeeded. Help must still satisfy its entirely local offline search requirement under HELP-05; using shared retrieval primitives must not make Help depend on a network embedding request. Route selection and availability of an optional local embedding model remain implementation decisions.')
 request(rag,'RAG-08','Proposed','Keep managed document contents and extracted text in local file storage, durable corpus/indexing metadata and jobs in SQLite, and document vectors in sqlite-vec with evidence/graph relationships in application-owned SQLite tables. Exact ownership, lexical indexing and consistency mechanics remain subject to STORE-03 and OPEN 08. Reuse common retrieval capabilities for documents, conventions and unified Knowledge without duplicating authoritative records. OxiRS is an evaluated candidate for selected reusable Rust components, not an approved additional store or replacement for SQLite, sqlite-vec, the router or the harness. Before selection, validate actual behavior, dependency/footprint impact, supported platforms, adapters, persistence, scope enforcement and recovery with representative documents; add no RDF/SPARQL service or third persistent store without an explicit architecture decision.')
 request(rag,'RAG-11','Confirmed','Newly added knowledge documents default to the current project. Users must be able to explicitly share a document across projects and move it to another project, including to correct adding it to the wrong project. Expose these controls in the document manager and through agent tools subject to configured permissions. Moving changes the current project association rather than requiring deletion and re-upload; preserve document identity, source provenance and attributed move history. The previous project must not retain future retrieval access solely because it was the original owner; any continued access must come from explicit sharing. Preserve existing historical evidence under its access rules rather than rewriting original provenance or claiming prior agent exposure can be undone. Adding documents without a current project and the precise sharing controls remain to specify.')
 request(rag,'RAG-12','Confirmed','Keep a DevWorks-managed copy of every imported knowledge document and treat it as a project artifact. Index and retrieve from this managed copy so moving or deleting the external original does not break the knowledge library. Retain the original source location as provenance without making retrieval depend on that path continuing to exist. Apply artifact identity, project scope, sharing, retention until explicit deletion and shared-reference preservation rules; link the document to its originating feature/task when applicable rather than inventing a work association for a project-only import. Document scope/move operations under RAG-11 must operate on the same managed document/artifact identity. Removing or rebuilding a search index does not delete the underlying artifact. Updating from a changed external original and replacement mechanics remain to specify; retain all managed versions until explicitly deleted under RAG-13.')
 paragraph(rag,'Source inspection on 1 November 2026 found a convention-focused RAG implementation in the referenced CodeGraph revision f602de72a782a3a069d0b1572b39142c0dbc44ee and the currently indexed afe73560215bbe7593fc59451de5cc3237e3eeca. ConventionEmbeddingService reads the conventions wiki section, uses markdown-aware chunks, combines BM25 with dense retrieval, and returns source revision and chunk metadata. It is exposed to agents and scheduled embedding ingestion. This is a useful existing baseline, not evidence of a general user-uploaded document library. In the multi-user TC.CodeGraphApi revision 1f95d38d883f88a9e6245e1278963a19df081b6e, RagIngestionService ingests Markdown sources with hashes, chunk metadata, model identity and dimensions; RagSearchService fuses full-text and dense candidates using reciprocal rank fusion. These sources were inspected, not built or runtime-tested. Existing migration scope remains projects, features, tasks and histories only; new document ingestion does not authorize importing old knowledge corpora.')
 paragraph(rag,'OxiRS assessment at commit 8a322740f820f94a509c888d8e3d0357ffd6010b: oxirs-graphrag exposes vector-index, embedding, SPARQL and LLM traits; its graph model uses RDF triples. oxirs-vec includes optional document content processing. These provide reuse candidates but do not demonstrate a ready adapter for the selected store or this app’s document workflow. The main GraphRAG engine keyword_search implementation generates SPARQL regular-expression/count scoring although its overview describes BM25. oxirs-chat also carries its own chat/provider and server dependencies. Do not infer retrieval quality, footprint or production suitability from advertised capabilities; suitability remains unvalidated. Source references: https://github.com/cool-japan/oxirs/blob/8a322740f820f94a509c888d8e3d0357ffd6010b/ai/oxirs-graphrag/src/lib.rs ; https://github.com/cool-japan/oxirs/blob/8a322740f820f94a509c888d8e3d0357ffd6010b/engine/oxirs-vec/Cargo.toml ; https://github.com/cool-japan/oxirs/blob/8a322740f820f94a509c888d8e3d0357ffd6010b/ai/oxirs-chat/Cargo.toml .')
 paragraph(rag,'CodeGraph reference paths: src/CodeGraph.Services/WikiRag/ConventionEmbeddingService.cs, MarkdownWikiChunker.cs, src/CodeGraph.Services/Assistant/CodeGraphMcpServer.cs and src/CodeGraph.Jobs/Jobs/IngestConventionEmbeddingsJob.cs at the revisions above. Multi-user reference paths: src/TC.CodeGraphApi.Services/Rag/RagIngestionService.cs and RagSearchService.cs. Optional source/retrieval algorithms may be reimplemented in Rust; the .NET services and their database/broker infrastructure must not become desktop prerequisites.')
 rag['blocks'].append(('h2','Document retrieval acceptance'))
 paragraph(rag,'Add user-owned Markdown, plain text, PDF and Word documents through the UI and an authorized agent tool; verify all four required formats are covered. Verify extracted passages and vectors become searchable, exact identifiers and paraphrased questions retrieve relevant evidence, and results open at the cited source revision/locator. Verify each import creates a managed project artifact. Move or delete its external original and verify the managed document remains retrievable and its provenance remains visible. Verify new documents default to the current project and remain isolated until explicitly shared. Move a mistakenly added document to another project; verify identity and provenance survive, the destination can retrieve it, and the prior project cannot retrieve it unless explicitly shared. Exercise scope-filter/cache reconciliation. Verify reviewer read-only access and instruction precedence. Edit, disable, remove and reindex a source; exercise failure, cancellation, provider unavailability, app restart and embedding-model changes without silent data loss, incompatible vector mixing or stale results presented as current. Inspect indexing logs and router usage. Verify vision extraction starts enabled in a new configuration and can be disabled in Settings. Exercise a mixed text/scanned document: extract existing text directly and route scanned pages through the configured vision model. Verify page-linked saved extraction is reused by later searches, source edits trigger refresh, and disabled/unavailable vision produces visible partial status. Verify indexed documents survive unrelated worktree cleanup and that index removal does not delete an external original. Evaluate retrieval against known relevant and irrelevant passages, including no-answer cases; the quality corpus and measurable acceptance thresholds remain to set. RAG 01–12; KNOW 01–08; STORE 01–06; ROUTE 01; HELP 05; ART 01–05.')
